blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:1891:\section{Formalization support for the register transport}
blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:1893:The statements of this section are not named results of the source article.  They isolate, as exact identities, the register bookkeeping that relates the six-register presentation used in Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary} to the two local extraction blocks $\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''$ and $\mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}'\mathrm{B}''$, and to the register order in which the auxiliary state is already known to be normalized.  Nothing here constructs an extraction isometry, and nothing here proves an approximation estimate: every identity below holds for arbitrary operators and arbitrary vectors, and the only hypotheses that appear are explicit isometry or unitarity equations for the operators involved.
blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:1898:	\uses{def:expanded-state}
blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:1899:	Reassociating the six registers into the two local blocks rewrites the register order $\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}'' \mid \mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}'\mathrm{B}''$ as the pair of blocks $(\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}')\mathrm{A}'' \mid (\mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}')\mathrm{B}''$.  This is a bijection between the index sets of the two presentations: it moves no register from one player to the other and permutes no register inside a block, so it is the identity on coordinates and only changes their grouping.
