blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:1907:	Moving the extracted register of each player to the front of that player's own block rewrites the register order $\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}'' \mid \mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}'\mathrm{B}''$ as $\mathrm{A}''\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}' \mid \mathrm{B}''\mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}'$.  This is a bijection between the index sets of the two presentations, and the induced permutation of coordinates is a linear isometric equivalence of the corresponding finite-dimensional Hilbert spaces.  It identifies neither player's original space with any other register.
